  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s financial contribution to the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) in the Occupied Palestinian Territories contributed to the provision of high-calorie food supplements, which were distributed to people with specific needs including pregnant and lactating women, and patients at ICRC-supported hospitals. Medical supplies and equipment, such as essential drugs and weapon-wound treatment kits, were provided to hospitals and other facilities providing health services across Gaza.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency aid and / or livelihood support were provided to Palestinian households allowing them to meet their daily needs and become more resilient to unrest in the PTs. Households that lost their source of income due to hostilities were provided with cash to help them start new income-generating activities. Cash or either supplies or equipment were provided to several households to assist them in the production of food.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICRC provided capacity-building assistance and various medical supplies and resources to several Palestinian emergency responders, including the Palestinian Red Crescent Society (PRCS) and the Artificial Limb and Polio Society (ALPC). The ICRC capacity-building assistance allowed the organisations to maintain and strengthen their operational response capacity. The beneficiary organisations continued to provide free physical rehabilitation services as a result of the contribution provided by ICRC with Australian funding. The funding was also used for ICRC to continue to support the Magen David Adom and the Palestine Red Crescent and help them coordinate their activities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Gaza, ICRC provided extensive assistance to the European Gaza Hospital, including staff training, specialist staff augmentation, provision of basic drugs and other essential supplies. To supplement the decreasing capacity of Gaza&apos;s hospitals as a result of the conflict, ICRC, in partnership with the Norwegian Red Cross, established the Rafa Field Hospital which played a crucial role in treating those affected by mass-casualty incidents and provided outpatient and emergency consultations, surgery, ante and postnatal care. Australia&apos;s funding to ICRC&#x2019;s health support in Gaza directly enabled 1,178 consultations and 95 surgical procedures.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social protection measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ICRC intervention allowed for improved access to water, electricity and sanitation services in the Gaza Strip through assistance in the facilitation of importing essential parts. The ICRC program enabled the service providers to become more resilient to unrest and the strict import limitations for essential goods needed for the service providers to operate efficiently. Palestinians also became better able to access essential health services in the Gaza Strip. ICRC&apos;s interventions allowed PRCS and other health providers to provide better and more efficient services through providing them with necessary capacity building and medical supplies and equipment.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
